# Concept Aliases

Canonical concept pages with their known aliases. When a downstream AI sees an aliased term, it should resolve to the canonical page. When the concept-frequency audit surfaces an alias, the alias is added to `SLUG_STOPS` to avoid resurfacing.

## How to add an alias

When triaging `wiki/CONCEPT-COVERAGE.md`, if a candidate is genuinely covered by an existing page under a different name:

1. Add a row to the alias table below — canonical page on the left, alias on the right.
2. Add the alias slug to `SLUG_STOPS` in `_scripts/concept-frequency-audit.py` with a `# ALIAS: <canonical>` comment.
3. Rerun the audit.

